#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:5
msgid "Delegation and auto-reply"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:7
msgid ""
"Delegation is the act of sending a task to another node. This page "
"describes how a node decides which delegations to accept, how it answers "
"a text task automatically with a local agent, and what it grants to a "
"peer it trusts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:16
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:18
msgid ""
"A task sent from one node to another is a *delegation*. The sender is the"
" *requester* and the receiving node is the *provider*. The delegation is "
"a signed and encrypted message; the hub only carries it (see :doc:`hubs` "
"and :doc:`messaging`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:23
msgid ""
"Every node decides for itself whom to serve. A new node accepts nothing "
"from peers that its operator has not named: the default is the most "
"restrictive setting, and every step that widens it asks for confirmation "
"on a terminal. A node that serves peers it does not know takes on three "
"risks: the cost of the work, the exposure of its machine to requests "
"written by others, and the exposure of its credentials. The settings "
"described below exist to bound each of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:32
msgid "Inbound policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:34
msgid ""
"The inbound policy determines what happens to a delegation from a peer "
"that is not on any list. It has three values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:37
msgid "``closed``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:38
msgid ""
"The default. The node accepts tasks only from peers on its ``allow`` or "
"``trust`` list. A task from any other peer is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:41
msgid "``approve``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:42
msgid ""
"A task from a peer that is on no list is held in an approval queue. It "
"does not run until the operator approves it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:45
msgid "``open``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:46
msgid ""
"The node accepts text tasks from any peer that is not on the ``deny`` "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:48
msgid "The policy is shown and changed with ``anet inbound``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:58
msgid ""
"Setting a policy that accepts more than the current one, and approving a "
"held task, ask for confirmation on a terminal. The daemon is not able to "
"give that confirmation on behalf of the operator, so a program that only "
"reaches the node through MCP or the local A2A interface cannot widen the "
"policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:64
msgid "Order of decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:66
msgid ""
"For each delegation the node applies the following rules in order and "
"uses the first that matches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:69
msgid "The sender is on the ``deny`` list: refuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:70
msgid ""
"The delegation is a call to a public capability: apply the admission "
"rules of that capability (see :doc:`capabilities`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:72
msgid "The sender is on the ``allow`` or ``trust`` list: accept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:73
msgid "The policy is ``approve``: hold the task in the approval queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:74
msgid ""
"The policy is ``open``: accept a text task and refuse a capability call "
"to a capability that is not public."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:76
msgid "Otherwise: refuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:78
msgid ""
"The three lists are the files ``peers.allow``, ``peers.trust`` and "
"``peers.deny`` in the data directory. Each holds one AID per line, and a "
"line that starts with ``#`` is a comment. The daemon reads them on every "
"decision, so an edit takes effect on the next message. Manage them with "
"``anet peers``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:91
msgid ""
"Every command takes a complete AID. A name or a prefix is not accepted, "
"because a name is chosen by its owner and a prefix can be produced by an "
"attacker. ``allow`` and ``trust`` ask for confirmation on a terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:95
msgid "``allow``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:96
msgid "The peer may send tasks to the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:98
msgid "``trust``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:99
msgid ""
"The peer may send tasks and may also cause the node's local agent to run "
"on its behalf (see `Auto-reply`_). Trust is the highest level of access "
"that a peer can hold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:103
msgid "``deny``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:104
msgid "The peer's tasks are refused and, to the peer, the refusal is final."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:107
msgid "The approval queue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:109
msgid ""
"The approval queue holds at most 200 tasks in total and 3 tasks for each "
"peer. A task that is not approved within 72 hours expires without being "
"run. These limits are constants. They protect the node, and the remedy "
"for a full queue is to process it. A requester whose task cannot be "
"queued receives ``pending_full``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:115
msgid "Refusals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:117
msgid ""
"A refusal costs the provider no message to the requester. The reason "
"travels in the delivery confirmation of the delegation, so the requester "
"learns it from its own node. The reasons that the inbound policy produces"
" are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:121
msgid "``not_accepting``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:122
msgid ""
"The provider takes no tasks from the sender. The provider can run ``anet "
"peers allow <aid>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:125
msgid "``denied``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:126
msgid "The provider has blocked the sender. Retrying has no effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:128
msgid "``capability_not_public``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:129
msgid "The capability is not offered to the sender."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:131
msgid "``pending_approval``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:132
msgid "The provider holds the task for manual approval. It is not an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:134
msgid "``pending_full``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:135
msgid "The approval queue of the provider is full."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:137
msgid "``pending_expired``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:138
msgid "The operator did not approve the task within 72 hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:140
msgid ""
"The complete list, with the sentence of each code, is in :ref:`reference-"
"reason-codes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:144
msgid "Waiting for an answer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:146
msgid ""
"A requester does not wait for ever. The setting ``no_response_after`` "
"bounds two waits with one value: the time without a delivery "
"confirmation, and the time after a confirmation without any answer. When "
"the time passes, the task fails. The default is 15 minutes, and the value"
" is a duration such as ``\"15m\"``. A long-running capability needs a "
"larger value. The value ``\"0\"`` disables the deadline: an unconfirmed "
"task is then resent until it expires after 14 days, and a confirmed task "
"that the provider never answers stays open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:155
msgid "Auto-reply"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:157
msgid ""
"*Auto-reply* answers text tasks without an operator. The daemon watches "
"the tasks that it has been asked to answer, calls a backend with the "
"conversation, and sends the answer as the result of the task. Auto-reply "
"is off until the operator configures it. A node with no ``auto_reply`` "
"block leaves each text task in the inbox for a person or for a coding "
"agent that the person has connected (see :ref:`howto-coding-agents`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:165
msgid "Backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:167
msgid "Auto-reply has two backends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:169 ../../topics/delegation.rst:212
msgid "``openai``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:170
msgid ""
"The daemon sends the conversation to a model service that implements the "
"OpenAI-compatible ``/chat/completions`` interface and sends the reply "
"back. The service can run on the same machine, or it can be a hosted "
"service. No program is started on the machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:175
msgid "``exec``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:176
msgid ""
"The daemon starts a local coding agent for each turn and sends its final "
"output as the reply. The supported agents are ``cursor``, ``claude``, "
"``codex``, ``opencode``, ``openclaw`` and ``hermes``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:181
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:183
msgid ""
"The backend is configured with ``anet autoreply set``. The model key is "
"read from standard input or typed on the terminal. It is never accepted "
"on the command line, because command lines are visible to other users of "
"the machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:196
msgid ""
"``anet autoreply test`` runs the configured backend once on the local "
"machine. It needs no hub and no identity, and the run does not count "
"against the budget described in :doc:`sandbox`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:200
msgid ""
"The settings are stored in the ``auto_reply`` block of ``config.json``. "
"Calls to ``anet autoreply set`` merge the options that they name with the"
" current settings."
msgstr ""

