msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:271
msgid "Who is answered, and how"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:273
msgid ""
"The ``exec`` backend decides how to run for each turn from the lists, "
"which it reads again on every turn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:276
msgid "A peer on the ``deny`` list is not answered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:277
msgid ""
"A peer on the ``trust`` list is answered according to ``trusted``. The "
"default is ``direct``. A directly run agent has the rights of the "
"operator's user, so trust in a peer is equal to giving that peer the "
"rights of the account that runs the daemon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:281
msgid ""
"Any other peer is answered according to ``untrusted``. The default "
"``off`` runs no program for the peer and leaves the task in the inbox. "
"The value ``sandbox`` runs the agent in the sandbox described in "
":doc:`sandbox`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:285
msgid ""
"A turn that is decided as ``sandbox`` never falls back to a direct run. "
"When the sandbox is unavailable, when the budget for the day is used up, "
"or when a resource limit is exceeded, the node does not start the agent, "
"and the requester receives a refusal with the reason "
"``sandbox_unavailable`` or ``budget``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:290
msgid ""
"The ``openai`` backend starts no local program, so the choice between "
"``direct`` and ``sandbox`` does not apply. Every turn for a peer that is "
"not trusted counts against the run budget, and when the budget is used up"
" the task is refused with ``budget``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:295
msgid ""
"A call to a capability is never answered by auto-reply. It is routed to "
"the service that provides the capability. Auto-reply handles text tasks "
"only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:298
msgid ""
"When the backend completes the task, the daemon sends the final reply as "
"part of the result, together with a receipt signed by the provider, and "
"the task ends. Otherwise the conversation continues in further messages, "
"with a limit of 30 automatic replies for each task. When the backend "
"fails, the requester receives the standard ``backend_failed`` sentence "
"and no text from the backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:305
msgid "Requesting a delegation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:307
msgid ""
"The requester side uses the same concepts. A text task is sent with "
"``anet delegate`` and a capability call with the ``--capability`` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:319
msgid ""
"``anet delegate`` returns the task at once. The task then moves through "
"the A2A states ``submitted``, ``working``, ``input-required`` and a final"
" state. ``anet task get`` shows the state, and ``anet inbox`` and ``anet "
"results`` list the tasks that others sent to the node and the tasks the "
"node sent that have ended. Receipts and the final text are verified "
"before they are shown as verified. See :doc:`messaging` for delivery "
"confirmation and :doc:`payments` for tasks that ask for payment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:328
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:330
msgid ""
"The default configuration accepts no work from strangers and starts no "
"program on behalf of a peer. Each widening is an explicit step on a "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:332
msgid ""
"``open`` makes the node reachable by everyone for text tasks. Combine it "
"with ``approve`` or with an ``untrusted`` value of ``off`` unless the "
"node runs on a machine that holds nothing of value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:335
msgid ""
"``trust`` is bound to an AID. An identity keeps its AID when its keys are"
" rotated, so the trust stays in place until the operator removes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:337
msgid ""
"The lists are plain files with the permissions ``0600``. Anyone who can "
"write them can change the policy, so the data directory must be readable "
"only by its owner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/delegation.rst:340
msgid ""
"The control token of the daemon is also a credential. A local program "
"that holds it can run an agent in the same way as the operator can."
msgstr ""

